==Central Franconian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|gmw-cfr|kumme}} {{i|some Ripuarian dialects, including Kölsch}}
* {{l|gmw-cfr|kun}}, {{l|gmw-cfr|kunn}}, {{l|gmw-cfr|konn}} {{i|Ripuarian; some Moselle Franconian dialects; chiefly dated}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|gmw-cfr}} {{m|goh|queman}}. The form is native in Moselle Franconian, but borrowed from {{etyl|de|gmw-cfr}} in Ripuarian.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkomə/|lang=gmw-cfr}}

===Verb===
{{head|gmw-cfr|verb|third-person singular present|kennt|or|kött|past tense|kom|past participle|komme|or|jekomme|or|gekomme}}

# to [[come]]

====Usage notes====
* The present conjugation in [[Moselle Franconian]] goes: ''du'' {{m|gmw-cfr|kenns}}, ''hä'' {{m|gmw-cfr|kennt}}, ''dir'' {{m|gmw-cfr|kommt}}.
* The present conjugation in [[Ripuarian]] goes: ''du'' {{m|gmw-cfr|köss}}, ''hä'' {{m|gmw-cfr|kött}}, ''ühr'' {{m|gmw-cfr|kott}}. These forms are vestiges of the old infinitive ''konn, kunn''.

